    "diff_hunk": "@@ -66240,6 +66242,24 @@ dictionary <dfn>ElementDefinitionOptions</dfn> {\n    <li><p>If <span>IsConstructor</span>(<var>constructor</var>) is false, then throw a\n    <code>TypeError</code> and abort these steps.</p></li>\n \n+   <li>\n+    <p>If <var>constructor</var> is an <span>interface object</span> whose corresponding\n+    interface either is <code>HTMLElement</code> or has <code>HTMLElement</code> in its set of\n+    <span>inherited interfaces</span>, throw a <code>TypeError</code> and abort these steps.</p>\n+\n+    <div class=\"note\">\n+     <p>This prevents passing, for example, <code>HTMLButtonElement</code> as\n+     <var>constructor</var>, and thus enabling the creation of <code>HTMLButtonElement</code>\n+     instances with a local name that is not <code>button</code>.</p>\n+\n+     <p><span data-x=\"interface object\">Interface objects</span> that do not inherit from\n+     <code>HTMLElement</code> (for example <code>TextTrack</code>), or classes defined in JavaScript\n+     (such as <code data-x=\"\">Set</code>), will pass this step without throwing a\n+     <code>TypeError</code>. However, they will later cause <span>create an element</span> to\n+     fail.</p>",
